// Declares a reactive context: `context #name(default)` binds `name`, and
// `name(value) { ... }` overrides it for a subtree. A context is ambient
// because the form that declares one has to be available wherever a package
// declares state, and the mark is what the checker matches — the name
// `context` is shadowable like any other.
//
// The context's type is its default's, which every provider's value is held
// to. A default whose type says too little -- `null`, an empty list -- is
// written as a typed const: `const nobody option[User] = null`, then
// `context #who(nobody)`.
//
// TODO Investigate type arguments at a call site, spelled with brackets as Go
// does (`context[option[User]] #who(null)`), which would state the type in
// place; `<…>` there is not LL(1) against a comparison.
#[_builtin(context)]
component context[V any, F any](default V) F {}
